    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1169">

                <pb facs="1080" n="822" xml:id="pg822"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111F23/17</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to the British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Spring Rice</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-01-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 29, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your notes of the 13th, 14th, and 17th instant in regard to the
                    steamer <hi rendition="#italic">KD–3</hi>, which entered the port of San Juan,
                    Porto Rico, in the possession of a German prize crew, and to inform you in reply
                    that, as stated to you informally at the Department, this Government, after a
                    careful investigation of the case, determined to treat the steamer as a tender
                    to a belligerent fleet, and on the 22d instant instructions were given that the
                    vessel be ordered to leave port within twenty-four hours after notice to that
                    effect, and upon failure to leave, that the vessel, together with the prize
                    officers and crew, be interned, the British officers and crew and the Chinese
                    seamen being released.</p>
                <p>The Department is now advised that the vessel, together with the prize officers
                    and crew, was interned on the 25th instant at San Juan.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
